# Files whose bytes are pinned by SHA-256 must never be rewritten on checkout.
#
# reports/prism_2026-08-14/PREREGISTRATION.json records the SHA-256 of the
# disease correspondence and the candidate review, so that a frozen
# pre-registration can be proven unchanged. Those hashes are taken over raw file
# bytes. With core.autocrlf enabled - the default on many Windows clones - git
# rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout, every hash changes, and the pin fails on a
# clean checkout even though nothing was edited.
#
# `-text` disables end-of-line conversion in both directions, so the bytes on
# disk are exactly the bytes in the object store. It does not rewrite anything
# already committed, which matters here: repairing this by regenerating the
# frozen pre-registration would mean editing it after scoring.
reports/prism_2026-08-14/*.json -text
reports/candidate_review_2026-08-01/CANDIDATE_REVIEW_60.csv -text
